## 3. Categorical Source Audit Summary

- **External Curriculum Items (`[UNVERIFIED]`):** The topics listed under the AlphaGrep × IIIT Hyderabad Winter School represent curriculum themes remembered and summarized from secondary public announcements. Because specific URLs, retrieval timestamps, and exact quoted passages were not inspected and logged in this session, they are formally labeled as **`[UNVERIFIED]` ("source not inspected")**.
- **Literature Citations ("recalled, not inspected"):** Citations to academic papers (e.g., Artzner et al. 1999, McNeil & Frey 2000, Auer et al. 2002, DeMiguel et al. 2009) represent standard literature recalled from knowledge. They are noted as **"recalled, not inspected"** until specific paper DOIs/pages are opened and cited.
- **Project Design Goals (`[INTERPRETATION]`):** Securitized products cash-flow waterfalls, EVT tail risk, and offline dashboards reflect pedagogical interpretations of the user's master specification.
- **Architectural & Integrity Choices (`[ENG_CHOICE]`):** The 6-part criteria taxonomy, anti-leakage runtime barriers, exact deterministic moment recursions, and `SeedSequence` RNG policies are rigorous engineering standards introduced for mathematical integrity.
